WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.160
There are two styles of communication, violent&nbsp;
and nonviolent — and a whole spectrum in between.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:15.440
Violent communication is coercive, manipulative&nbsp;
and hurts.It includes making generalizations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:21.440
and a use of language that induces fear,shame or&nbsp;
guilt.It is often ineffective since it diverts our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:27.040
attention away from clarifying our actual needs&nbsp;
and distracts us from solving the actual conflict.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:35.440
Nonviolent Communication is based on the idea that&nbsp;
we all share universal human desires such as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:41.600
need for trust, safety,and appreciation.It&nbsp;
allows us to empathize and think clearly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.400
And as a result, reach a better and&nbsp;
more honest understanding of each other.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:58.880
Nonviolent Communication follows 4 steps:&nbsp;
observation,feeling,needs and requests.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.280
To understand how it works, let’s imagine&nbsp;
a college student being late for class.Old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:10.880
Jay, her former teacher,would usually&nbsp;
have just said “and here she comes again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:16.960
late Ann.”In class he then would give her a hard&nbsp;
time and after - as his form of punishment - a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:21.440
bunch of senseless assignments.Then, both&nbsp;
would often feel bad for the rest of the day.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.400
New Jay, who’s her current teacher,&nbsp;
learned about Nonviolent Communication&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.800
and knows that it begins with a clear observation.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.600
During observation he tries noticing&nbsp;
concrete facts - things that happen at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:43.040
that very moment.New Jay jots down that Ann&nbsp;
arrived 20 minutes late and that his pulse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.679
is up- possibly a sign of stress.Note that&nbsp;
sharing observations should not be combined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.679 --> 00:01:46.480
with evaluating them, because then others&nbsp;
can hear criticism and naturally resist.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:51.840
When focusing on his feelings, New Jay connects&nbsp;
with his heart and can learn to understand various&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:58.320
underlying emotions.This is important because what&nbsp;
seems to be anger,might in fact be sadness.During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:04.560
this step it is essential to distinguish feelings&nbsp;
from thoughts.After class, New Jay shares his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.200
observation and explains to Ann that he feels&nbsp;
disrespected when someone is late for his class.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.720
Knowing his needs is important&nbsp;
because it allows him to enrich&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:19.200
his life , and feel at peace. If we&nbsp;
disregard our needs or don't live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:24.080
up to our values,we experience stress&nbsp;
and frustration.Understanding that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.320
all have universal human needs is perhaps&nbsp;
the most important step in the process.New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:35.840
Jay tells Ann that they should find a way&nbsp;
to respect each other's values and desires.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.520
Lastly there is the Request which clarifies&nbsp;
what future New Jay wants for himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.640
and this relationship.Clear requests are hence&nbsp;
crucial to a transformative communication.When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:52.320
we ask for concrete actions, we often find&nbsp;
creative ways to ensure that everyone’s needs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:58.080
are met. New Jay asks Ann not to come to class at&nbsp;
all, if she happens to run later than 1 minute.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.240
Marshall Rosenberg, who developed the&nbsp;
model, liked to show the differences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:09.440
between the communication styles with two&nbsp;
animals.The Jackal was a symbol of aggression,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:14.400
dominance and violent communication.The&nbsp;
Giraffe with his long neck and big heart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.200
represents a clear-sighted and compassionate&nbsp;
speaker and nonviolent communication style.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.560
"All violence”, Rosenberg wrote, “is the result&nbsp;
of people tricking themselves into believing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:31.840
that their pain derives from other people and that&nbsp;
consequently those people deserve to be punished.”

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:36.240
What are your thoughts on this model?&nbsp;
